    blurb: 'Its website lists residential fencing, commercial fencing, and automatic gate installation.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Modern Stone and Masonry',
    url: 'https://blockwallstgeorgeutah.com/',
    where: 'St. George, Utah, serving Washington County',
    blurb: 'Its website lists block fence walls, 6-foot block walls, and block wall repair, along with stonemasonry, stucco, concrete flatwork, pavers, and flagstone. It says it has served the St. George area for over 10 years.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Robinson Fencing',
    url: 'https://robinsonfences.com/',
    where: 'Cedar City, Utah, serving Southern Utah',
    blurb: 'Its website lists residential and commercial chain-link, commercial security fencing, privacy link, and vinyl fencing, and mentions free estimates across Southern Utah and financing options.',
  },
  {
    name: 'St George Deck and Fence',
    url: 'https://stgeorgedeckandfence.com/',
    where: 'St. George, Utah',
    blurb: 'Its website lists residential and commercial fencing and fence installation and repair, alongside residential decks, pool decks, and deck repair.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Taylor Made Fencing',
    url: 'https://taylormadefencing.com/',
    where: 'Washington, Utah',
    blurb: 'Its website lists chain link, ranch or field, vinyl, wood or pole, and temporary fencing.',
  },
];

const faq = [
  {
    question: 'Who are the fence companies in St. George, UT?',
    answer: 'Local fence and wall businesses that appear in St. George searches include Kirklands Fence & Garden, St George Deck and Fence, Taylor Made Fencing (Washington, UT), Robinson Fencing (Cedar City, UT), and, for block walls, Modern Stone and Masonry. This is an unranked, alphabetical list based on what each company\'s own website states, not an endorsement.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I choose between fence companies?',
    answer: 'Compare at least two or three written quotes on the same scope, verify each company\'s Utah license status and insurance yourself, ask about warranty and who pulls the permit, and look at completed work. A price far below the others usually means a different scope.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Are the companies on this page paying to be listed?',
    answer: 'No. Listings are not paid placements, and the order is alphabetical. If a listed company ever becomes a paying partner of this site, this page will say so.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which company should I pick for a block wall?',
    answer: 'Ask any masonry company to describe the footing, reinforcement, and drainage in writing, and confirm who pulls the permit. St. George City Code §10-18-5 requires a permit for retaining walls of 4 feet or more and for any fence or retaining wall in a front setback.',
  },
