---

<GuideLayout
  title="Fence & Wall Pros in St. George"
  description="Local fence and block wall companies serving St. George, UT, listed alphabetically from their own websites, plus a checklist for choosing between them."
  path={path}
  eyebrow="Local companies · St. George & Washington County"
  h1="Fence and Block Wall Companies Serving St. George, UT"
  answer="As of September 2026, local fence and wall businesses that come up for St. George include Kirklands Fence & Garden, St George Deck and Fence, Taylor Made Fencing, Robinson Fencing, and, for block walls, Modern Stone and Masonry. This list is alphabetical and drawn from each company's own website; it is not a ranking or an endorsement."
  updated="2026-09-26"
  updatedLabel="September 26, 2026"
  faq={faq}
  extraNodes={[
    itemListSchema({
      path,
      name: 'Fence and block wall companies serving St. George, UT',
      items: companies.map((c) => ({ name: c.name, url: c.url, description: `${c.where}. ${c.blurb}` })),
    }),
  ]}
  related={[
    { href: '/fence-and-block-wall-cost-st-george-ut/', label: 'Cost guide', blurb: 'What to expect before you request quotes.' },
    { href: '/fence-permit-st-george-ut/', label: 'Permit rules', blurb: 'Questions to ask about who pulls the permit.' },
    { href: '/fence-installation-st-george-ut/', label: 'Fence installation', blurb: 'Vetting checklist and red flags.' },
    { href: '/block-wall-installation-st-george-ut/', label: 'Block wall installation', blurb: 'What to ask a masonry company.' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Most homeowners get two or three quotes, and it helps to know who is out there. These are fence and wall businesses
    serving St. George and Southern Utah that we could confirm were operating with a live website as of September 26, 2026. The
    descriptions below repeat only what each company's own site says. We have not inspected their work, checked their
    licenses, or verified their claims, and this is not a complete list of every company in the area.
  </p>

  <h2>Companies, in alphabetical order</h2>
  <ul>
    {companies.map((c) => (
      <li>
        <strong><a href={c.url} rel="noopener">{c.name}</a></strong> — {c.where}. {c.blurb}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="sgfw-callout">
    <strong>How this list was built.</strong> Listings are not paid placements, and none of these companies has any
    arrangement with this site as of the update date above. Order is alphabetical, not ranked, and we show no ratings or
    reviews because we have none of our own to verify. If that changes, this page will say so.
  </div>

  <h2>How to choose between them</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Price the same scope.</strong> Write down material, height, total feet, gates, removal, and cleanup, and give the same list to each company.</li>
    <li><strong>Verify the license yourself.</strong> Search each company in the <a href="https://dopl.utah.gov/" rel="noopener">Utah Division of Professional Licensing</a> lookup. Do not rely on a website's claim, ours or theirs.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirm insurance directly</strong> with the insurer or agent, and ask for a certificate.</li>
    <li><strong>Ask about permits and HOA paperwork.</strong> Find out who prepares the site plan and who submits. See the <a href="/fence-permit-st-george-ut/">permit guide</a> and <a href="/hoa-fence-requirements-st-george-ut/">HOA guide</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Look at completed work,</strong> ideally a few years old, and ask for references you can call.</li>
    <li><strong>Compare warranties in writing,</strong> covering workmanship and materials separately.</li>
    <li><strong>Check specialty fit.</strong> A company that mostly does chain-link may not be the right pick for a reinforced block retaining wall, and a masonry company may not do wood privacy fences. Ask.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Questions to ask every company</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>How long until you can start, and how long will the job take?</li>
    <li>Who is on site, employees or subcontractors?</li>
    <li>What is the payment schedule?</li>
    <li>How do you set posts in my soil, and how deep?</li>
    <li>What happens if the permit requires a change?</li>
    <li>What is not included in this quote?</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="sgfw-note">
    Company details are as described on each company's website on September 26, 2026, and may have changed. Names are used only to identify the
    businesses. Listing here is not an endorsement, and no company on this page is affiliated with this site.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
